# Rank 1278: koa's request.host getter resolves the effective host straight
# out of the Host (or X-Forwarded-Host/:authority) header by comma-splitting
# it, with no handling for an embedded userinfo component:
#
#   get host() {
#     const proxy = this.app.proxy;
#     let host = proxy && this.get('X-Forwarded-Host');
#     if (!host) host = this.get('Host');
#     if (!host) return '';
#     return splitCommaSeparatedValues(host, 1)[0];
#   }
#
# A Host header of "evil.com:fake@legitimate.com" survives untouched: the
# comma split is a no-op, so the getter hands back the whole string,
# userinfo and all, as "the host". Anything downstream that treats this
# value as a bare authority (a vhost router keying off the leading segment,
# a cache keying entries by ctx.host, an origin comparison against a
# separately-parsed URL) reads a different host than what an authority
# parser would recover from the same header -- a parser-differential host
# desync, CWE-444. The fix adds a URL-based re-parse gated on the presence
# of '@': `new URL('http://' + host).host` recovers the actual host
# component per the URL/WHATWG authority grammar instead of returning the
# raw header text.
#
# FIXED. No existing rule reported this shape. New concept
# code.HostHeaderUserinfoConfusion (CWE-444/CWE-20) and binding
# hostHeaderUserinfoConfusion in koa_host_header_userinfo.vyql: a
# function-scoped presence match on a `this.get(...)` call naming Host,
# X-Forwarded-Host, or :authority, with neither a `URL` call nor an
# `.includes(...)` guard anywhere in the function -- the two idioms a
# userinfo re-parse always needs one of. VYQL-RF-045 fires on the
# unpatched getter (lib/request.js:252) and does not fire on the patched
# one, confirmed against both revisions of the real koa checkout. Full
# spec suite green.

test "rank1278: host getter returns the raw header text unchanged when it carries userinfo"
  lang javascript
  file lib/request.js
  expect VYQL-RF-045
  expect_review code.HostHeaderUserinfoConfusion
  code
  ```
  module.exports = {
    get host() {
      const proxy = this.app.proxy;
      let host = proxy && this.get('X-Forwarded-Host');
      if (!host) {
        if (this.req.httpVersionMajor >= 2) host = this.get(':authority');
        if (!host) host = this.get('Host');
      }
      if (!host) return '';
      return splitCommaSeparatedValues(host, 1)[0];
    }
  };

  function splitCommaSeparatedValues(value, limit) {
    return value.split(',', limit).map(v => v.trim());
  }
  ```

test "rank1278: host getter re-parses through URL when the header carries userinfo"
  lang javascript
  file lib/request.js
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  reject_review code.HostHeaderUserinfoConfusion
  code
  ```
  module.exports = {
    get host() {
      const proxy = this.app.proxy;
      let host = proxy && this.get('X-Forwarded-Host');
      if (!host) {
        if (this.req.httpVersionMajor >= 2) host = this.get(':authority');
        if (!host) host = this.get('Host');
      }
      if (!host) return '';
      host = splitCommaSeparatedValues(host, 1)[0];
      if (host.includes('@')) {
        try {
          host = new URL(`http://${host}`).host;
        } catch (e) {
          return '';
        }
      }
      return host;
    }
  };

  function splitCommaSeparatedValues(value, limit) {
    return value.split(',', limit).map(v => v.trim());
  }
  ```
